# <emoji> <type>(<scope>): <subject>
#
# <body>
#
# <footer>
#
# Emoji: REQUIRED. See .claude/references/gitmoji.md for the canonical
#   Gitmoji-to-type mapping. Common ones: ✨ feat, 🐛 fix, 📝 docs,
#   ♻️ refactor, ⚡️ perf, ✅ test, 🔧 chore, 👷 ci, 📦️ build, 💥 breaking.
# Type: feat|fix|docs|style|refactor|perf|test|chore|ci|build|revert
# Scope: (optional) component, module, or area affected
# Subject: imperative mood, max 72 chars, no period
#
# Body (optional): explain what and why, wrap at 72 chars
#
# Footer (optional):
# - Closes #123
# - BREAKING CHANGE: description
# - Co-Authored-By: Name <email>
#
# Examples:
# ✨ feat(auth): add password reset endpoint
# 🐛 fix(api): handle null response from external service
# 📝 docs(readme): update installation instructions
# ♻️ refactor(db): extract query builder to separate module
# ⚡️ perf(api): cache lookup results to halve p95 latency
# ✅ test(auth): cover token-refresh edge cases
# 🔧 chore(deps): bump fastapi to 0.115.6
# 👷 ci: pin actions/checkout to commit SHA
# 💥 feat!: drop support for Node 18
#
# ---
# Write your commit message above this line.
# Remove all comments and examples before committing.
# ---
